    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "UNITED\nAIRLINEJ\nFLY\nOVERNIGHT!..\nDIRECT to SUNNY CALIFORNIA\nUNITED - SHORTEST NEW YORK-CHICAGO\nFLY THE MAIN LINE\nThe Pioneer Coast-to-Coast Airway\nEffective Nov. 1st, 1938\nPlease destroy old schedule",
      "United's MAIN LINE Airway\n• TO ALASKA\nWANCOUVER\nG A\nTO THE\nORIEN\nTO THE\nORIEN\nSEATTLE\nTACOMA\nGlacier -\nSPOKANE\nRainier\nPORTLAND\nWALLA\nPENDLETON\nMINNEAPOLIS\nI PAUL\nDFORD\nBOISE\nMILWAUKE\nGrand\nTeton\nDude\nRanches\nCHEYENNE\nRIFORD\nTO EUROP\nTO HAWAII\nTHE ORIENT\n- OAKLAND\nSACRAMENTO\nOMAHA\nLINCOLN\nMOISES\nYosemite\nDENVER\n) COLORADO SPRINGS\nIOWA\nMOLINE\nSTROLLS\nAKRON\nSAN FRANCISCO\nELKO\nSALY\nEstes |\nPark\nCedar\nBreaks\nLAKE\na Zion\nBoulder Dam\nNAPOLIS\nKANSAS CITY\nTOLEDO\nOLUMBU\nPITTSBURGH\nEINCINNATI\nNEW YORK\nPHILADELPHIA\nCAMDEN\nSHINGTON\nLOUISVILLE\nLEM\nTO\n\u003e BERMUDA\nHASHVILLE\nCHATTANOOG\nOKLAHOMA CITY\nALBVOUCI\nTO HAWAII\nTHE ORIENT\nSANTA BARBARA\nLOS ANGELES.\nLONG BEACH\nSAN DIEGO\nGrand\nCanyon\nPHOENIX\nBRRLINCAHAME\nCHARLESTON:\nO MONTGOMERY\nFORT WORT\nUNITED\nAIR LINES\nFlight\nCode\nTo Mexico City\nNEW ORLEANS\nGALVESTON O\nBROWNILLE\nTo Mexico City, Central and South America\nUNITED AIR LINES\nConnecting Air Lines\nI Rail Lines ...... Highways\n• National Parks\nST PETERSBURGIO\nONASSAU\nTo Cuba, Central and\nouth America\nDeveloped from 125 mil-\nlion miles experience\n1. Safety is given first considera-\ntion in every operation.\n2. Flight dispatching and control\nare based on complete data\nsupplied by Federal Airways and\nUnited's meteorologists.\n3. Pilots do not fly when weather\nUnited's pilots\nis uncertain-\nare paid whether they fly or not.\n4. Trips are always flown in the\nsmooth upper levels, far above\nthe ground. Automatic barographs\ncontinuously record altitudes.\n5. A reserve of power and fuel\nfar in excess of requirements.\nMainliner -\n* United's Main line airway is the\noldest coast-to-coast route by ten\nyears... Over it United has lown\n25,000 coast-to-coast trips; 45,000\nNew York Chicago flights; 40,000\nLos Angeles - San Francisco flights.\ncago and the East with all major\nPacific Coast cities. . . overnight\nsleeper and scenic day flights be-\ntween East and \"Everywhere West\".\n* United's famous Douglas- built\nMainliners fly the Main Line.\nLuxurious sleepers on overnight\nflights.. deluxe 14 passenger Sky-\nlounges (exclusive with United) on\nlong-run daylight schedules... 21-\npassenger club planes on inter-city\nflights. These giant Mainliners cruise\nthree miles a minute at 55% power.\n* Your flight is backed by United's\nrigid flight code, developed from\n125,000,000 miles experience. . .\nand you enjoy United's famous\npersonalized service to passengers."
    ],
